WEBVTT

00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:07.690
"Little kitty, little kitty, why do your whiskers extend so far?

00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:10.360
Meow, meow."

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:12.990
Hmm, maybe me-meow would be better.

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:16.270
Oh no!

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:17.450
You gotta be kidding!

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:18.450
Come back!

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:25.040
Oh, you're the Student Body President,

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:27.000
Jin Kisaragi...

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.960
Would this happen to be yours?

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:31.340
Y-Yes. Th-Thank you.

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:35.340
I'm a freshman here. The name's Noel Vermillion.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:36.260
Noel?

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:40.180
So you're the one who blew away the previous record on the Ars Magus aptitude test.

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:44.980
Thank you very much.

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:46.350
S-Sure.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:51.440
<i>"Little kitty, little kitty, why do your whiskers extend so far?</i>

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:52.970
<i>Meow, meow."</i>

00:00:55.820 --> 00:00:57.530
<i>He saw it, didn't he?</i>

00:00:57.530 --> 00:00:59.280
<i>He read it for sure...</i>

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.960
No!

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:37.130
Rebel 4: Probabilistic Events

00:02:37.130 --> 00:02:40.470
You just <i>had</i> to be a pain in
my ass, didn't you, Hakumen?

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:44.100
I believe I told you not to get in my way.

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:46.640
Well, I hope you're comfy because you're gonna be stuck here for a while.

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:49.190
And I believe <i>I</i> told <i>you</i>

00:02:49.190 --> 00:02:51.940
that I don't take orders from anyone.

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:58.320
Oh? You're still able to move?

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:01.740
Guess the credit goes to your Power of Order.

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:03.160
But that don't mean shit.

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:06.080
This barrier is self-repairing.

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:10.250
A grandiose device used to just hold me, Grimalkin.

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:14.670
I'd send your ass flying back to the Boundary pronto if I could,

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:18.340
but I need that body of yours first: the Susano'o Unit.

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:22.380
Your manner speech is reminiscent of your mother.

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:24.050
Blood always tells.

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:26.890
Shut up.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:29.980
You've done well to come.

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:32.350
It has been a long time. Or has it?

00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:34.940
Affirmative. Based on your perception of time,

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:40.320
it has been 19,792 hours, 41 minutes, and 52 seconds since we last met.

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:47.240
For us, it has been 283,875 hours, 18 minutes, and 24 seconds.

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:52.210
Why did you unleash the Tsukuyomi Unit?

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:55.750
If you hadn't stopped it, all would've been reduced to ashes

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:58.340
and the irregularity would've been dealt with at the same time.

00:03:58.340 --> 00:04:00.920
We request your reason for unleashing it.

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:03.510
I am not obligated to answer you.

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:06.260
Your events are your own.

00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:08.970
We acknowledge your refusal to answer.

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:13.350
You're the ones who've released Yuuki Terumi from his cage in the Boundary, aren't you?

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:14.560
Affirmative.

00:04:14.770 --> 00:04:18.480
The process leading to the Day of Ruin has already been set in motion.

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:22.070
Don't tell me you all intend to make naught of the world?

00:04:22.070 --> 00:04:22.900
Negative.

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:24.950
We, the Takamagahara, only care that the world be correct.

00:04:24.950 --> 00:04:27.280
With the appearance of the Azure Successor,

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:34.210
the world has gone down the path of the probabilistic Continuum Shift.

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:38.290
We will control the event distortions that are likely to occur in the future

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:41.760
as well as target irregularities for elimination.

00:04:43.130 --> 00:04:45.220
Do you suddenly fancy yourselves gods?

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:46.430
Negative.

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:49.930
The Takamagahara is a man-made construct.

00:04:49.930 --> 00:04:53.020
Nothing created by men can equal the gods.

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:56.480
The Master Unit is no exception.

00:04:56.480 --> 00:05:01.030
With the way the Master Unit introduces distortions to the world, its existence is unnecessary.

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:03.900
You plan to use Terumi to that end?

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:07.030
Is he someone you are capable of handling, I wonder.

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:09.830
He is under our control.

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:12.410
He does not pose any measurable risk.

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:16.210
Should the occasion call for it, we will merely reinitialize him.

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:20.420
Rachel Alucard, you are close to our side.

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:22.340
Do you have any interest in coming back?

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:25.550
Your offer insults me.

00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:28.640
Observed.

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:33.220
We determine that answer to mean that you have no intention of returning to us.

00:05:33.970 --> 00:05:36.100
That choice is illogical.

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:41.940
Those who see everything are the ones who are the most blind.

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:49.280
Sh-Shit!

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:50.780
I wanna play.

00:05:50.780 --> 00:05:52.990
But we'll get told off again.

00:05:52.990 --> 00:05:54.830
It's chow time, Good Guy!

00:05:56.830 --> 00:06:00.000
H-Hey, are you sure this is okay to eat?

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:04.510
Kaka cuisine is both meowthwatering and mewtritious!

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:07.090
Eat lots so you get all better quick!

00:06:07.970 --> 00:06:09.800
It's hot!

00:06:13.220 --> 00:06:15.310
Hey, this ain't half bad.

00:06:20.690 --> 00:06:22.310
Second Lieutenant Noel Vermillion.

00:06:22.310 --> 00:06:23.480
Y-Yes, ma'am!

00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:24.690
My apologies, ma'am!

00:06:24.690 --> 00:06:26.530
I've had a lot on my mind, lately.

00:06:26.530 --> 00:06:28.360
Please forgive me.

00:06:29.610 --> 00:06:32.370
Never change, Noel.

00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:34.910
Did you seriously not know how it was?

00:06:34.910 --> 00:06:36.700
Noel, it's me!

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:39.120
M-Makoto?!

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:44.170
Makoto! Makoto!

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:48.880
This fluffy tail! No doubt about it. It's you, Makoto!

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:51.300
You need the tail to tell?!

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:55.930
Sounds like you've had it rough.

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:57.470
Yeah.

00:06:57.470 --> 00:07:00.310
I don't know what to do on my own...

00:07:00.310 --> 00:07:02.730
I'm so glad to see <i>you</i> here!

00:07:02.730 --> 00:07:06.480
By the way, Noel, were you okay when that thing happened?

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:07.360
What thing?

00:07:07.610 --> 00:07:11.450
You know, when the sky turned all bright and everything shook a lot.

00:07:11.450 --> 00:07:14.070
I-It did? And the sky turned bright?

00:07:14.070 --> 00:07:15.490
You didn't see it?

00:07:15.490 --> 00:07:18.540
Oh, no. I was on a lower level at the time.

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:21.210
All of Kagutsuchi was in an uproar.

00:07:21.210 --> 00:07:24.710
It's still pretty chaotic up at the top and there's no reliable info whatsoever,

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:27.590
but word on the street has it that it might've been the Takemikazuchi.

00:07:27.590 --> 00:07:29.210
The Takemikazuchi?

00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:32.300
A Nox Nyctores that played a part in the Dark War.

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:35.140
It's said that it was so powerful that they sealed it away afterwards—

00:07:35.140 --> 00:07:38.560
Wait, wasn't it you who told me that?

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:41.520
That must've been Tsubaki.

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:44.520
I think it was when we were studying for our first test ever.

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:49.030
Let's see...

00:07:49.030 --> 00:07:51.820
In order for mankind to be able to fight the Black Beast,

00:07:51.820 --> 00:07:55.910
they fused magic with science to create "ars magus".

00:07:55.910 --> 00:07:56.280
Was your paper on ars magus, Tsubaki?

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:58.490
Ugh, I don't know any of this...

00:07:58.790 --> 00:08:01.540
Yes. I wrote it in my spare time.

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:06.460
Hey, Noel, what's this Takemikazuchi thing here?

00:08:06.460 --> 00:08:07.880
Uh, um...

00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:10.380
It's the most famous Nox Nyctores of them all.

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:13.760
It was put to use against the Black Beast during the Dark War.

00:08:14.180 --> 00:08:18.430
But it was deemed too powerful and it's said it was sealed away.

00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:23.230
Those Nox Nyctores thingamajigs were made for fighting the Black Beast, right?

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:29.230
Yes, they were created by the great mage Nine, of the Six Heroes.

00:08:29.860 --> 00:08:31.570
Powerful Causality Weapons.

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:33.490
The Six Heroes used them to defeat the Black Beast.

00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:37.570
You learn that in elementary school, you know.

00:08:38.030 --> 00:08:40.790
Maybe where <i>you</i> went.

00:08:40.790 --> 00:08:44.540
I only got in because of my physical abilities.

00:08:44.540 --> 00:08:47.960
That's why I'm here giving you tips.

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:49.210
Yes, ma'am.

00:08:51.960 --> 00:08:55.300
We always used to hang out at the Military Academy library.

00:08:55.510 --> 00:08:56.260
Sure did.

00:08:56.260 --> 00:08:57.470
Oh, that's right!

00:08:57.470 --> 00:09:00.310
That one time, the Major—Jin Kisaragi came by!

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:05.270
Spill the beans, Noel! Did you really
choose secretary as your preferred post?

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:06.560
Did you?

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:07.850
Y-Yeah.

00:09:07.850 --> 00:09:10.690
You're so talented for ars magus, though.

00:09:10.690 --> 00:09:12.230
Yeah, but...

00:09:15.240 --> 00:09:17.110
S-Student Body President!

00:09:18.070 --> 00:09:19.410
Jin!

00:09:20.490 --> 00:09:22.950
Hey, Tsubaki. Studying hard?

00:09:22.950 --> 00:09:24.080
Y-Yes!

00:09:24.080 --> 00:09:25.370
With my roommates.

00:09:34.130 --> 00:09:36.800
Jin? What's wrong?

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:38.220
O-Oh, sorry.

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:39.850
Is something the matter?

00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:40.970
Not at all.

00:09:40.970 --> 00:09:42.510
I'll be excusing myself now.

00:09:42.930 --> 00:09:43.720
Okay.

00:09:47.560 --> 00:09:49.480
I wonder what's bothering him.

00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:52.690
Still got the hots for him, I take it.

00:09:53.570 --> 00:09:54.070
Wha—

00:09:54.280 --> 00:09:56.900
You can't fool us. Right, Noel?

00:09:56.900 --> 00:09:58.410
Really?! She does?!

00:09:58.700 --> 00:10:01.070
I-I keep telling you it's not true!

00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:03.540
That sure brings back memories.

00:10:04.910 --> 00:10:06.540
I wonder how Tsubaki's doing these days.

00:10:08.710 --> 00:10:09.500
Makoto?

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:13.250
She's on her way to Kagutsuchi.

00:10:13.250 --> 00:10:14.340
Really?!

00:10:14.340 --> 00:10:15.510
Yeah...

00:10:16.590 --> 00:10:19.300
But don't get too excited.

00:10:20.590 --> 00:10:24.850
This is top secret, even within
the Intelligence Department,

00:10:25.350 --> 00:10:27.230
but I feel you should know about this, Noel.

00:10:27.430 --> 00:10:28.810
Jin Kisaragi...

00:10:28.810 --> 00:10:31.940
The Major snuck out of the hospital and is on the run.

00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:34.610
B-But why?

00:10:34.610 --> 00:10:36.280
Besides, he's gravely wounded.

00:10:36.490 --> 00:10:37.860
No one knows.

00:10:38.360 --> 00:10:41.870
The brass thinks he defected.

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:43.200
No way!

00:10:46.370 --> 00:10:48.870
<i>Because of him...</i>

00:10:49.250 --> 00:10:51.710
That's not even the worst of it.

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:56.420
Hey, Noel, do you know what unit Tsubaki's attached to now?

00:10:58.220 --> 00:10:59.470
It's the Zeroth Squadron.

00:11:13.310 --> 00:11:15.070
The Wings of Justice.

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:17.400
The enforcement unit?!

00:11:19.360 --> 00:11:23.740
Tsubaki has been given orders to find Major Kisaragi and you, Noel,

00:11:24.200 --> 00:11:25.780
and terminate them.

00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:41.130
...you are tasked to seek out Major Jin Kisaragi and Second Lieutenant Noel Vermillion...

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:43.140
...and eliminate them.

00:11:43.140 --> 00:11:46.810
Our information says they are both currently on the run in Kagutsuchi.

00:11:46.810 --> 00:11:48.310
Uh, um...

00:11:48.310 --> 00:11:50.850
What have they done to deserve this?

00:11:51.390 --> 00:11:53.020
This is an Imperial Command.

00:11:54.350 --> 00:11:57.610
You aren't doubting the will of the Imperator, are you?

00:11:57.610 --> 00:11:58.980
N-No, sir.

00:11:59.190 --> 00:12:04.700
However, it would not seem wise to allow your doubts to manifest in your sword,

00:12:05.490 --> 00:12:06.490
so in brief...

00:12:06.490 --> 00:12:08.410
The rebel, Ragna the Bloodedge.

00:12:08.790 --> 00:12:10.120
The Grim Reaper?

00:12:10.370 --> 00:12:13.580
It appears that Major Kisaragi and Second Lieutenant Vermillion

00:12:13.580 --> 00:12:16.960
both had contact with that man
and subsequently defected.

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:19.800
The branch office has
suffered catastrophic losses.

00:12:20.170 --> 00:12:25.140
It seems the two of them share some kind of special relationship with that man.

00:12:25.140 --> 00:12:26.340
That can't be...

00:12:26.340 --> 00:12:27.430
That is all.

00:12:27.430 --> 00:12:30.810
You are free to go, First Lieutenant Tsubaki Yayoi.

00:13:01.960 --> 00:13:04.260
The sealed Armagus Izayoi.

00:13:04.260 --> 00:13:07.510
I never thought I'd use this against those two...

00:13:18.940 --> 00:13:20.020
Jin...

00:13:26.820 --> 00:13:29.200
Wait for me, Brother. I'm...

00:13:30.740 --> 00:13:33.250
It's just a flesh wound...

00:13:36.160 --> 00:13:38.380
Oh, dear, he's a ragged mess.

00:13:38.380 --> 00:13:42.460
Perhaps too great a handicap, even for the great Hero?

00:13:42.460 --> 00:13:44.050
You gonna help him?

00:13:46.840 --> 00:13:49.720
It appears that this is not meant to be my scene.

00:13:58.560 --> 00:14:00.610
Long time no see, Jin.

00:14:00.980 --> 00:14:04.570
Do not address me so familiarly, damn cat. I do not know you.

00:14:05.740 --> 00:14:08.910
Well, that's fine. The name's Jubei.

00:14:09.280 --> 00:14:10.070
Jubei?

00:14:10.450 --> 00:14:13.200
Play games with me, will you?
Claiming to be one of the Six Heroes.

00:14:13.580 --> 00:14:16.290
Well yer free to call me whatever ye like.

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:19.170
I got a message fer ye from a certain someone.

00:14:19.670 --> 00:14:22.630
The world is constantly striving fer parity.

00:14:22.630 --> 00:14:26.130
If things start tiltin' one way, a power to correct that tilt will also appear.

00:14:26.130 --> 00:14:28.760
And <i>that's</i> the Power of Order.

00:14:28.760 --> 00:14:30.220
What are you saying?

00:14:30.550 --> 00:14:34.810
The farther things tilt, the greater that power.

00:14:34.810 --> 00:14:37.810
Enough to put the world itself in jeopardy.

00:14:39.390 --> 00:14:42.730
The Power of Order itself is neither good nor evil.

00:14:42.730 --> 00:14:45.110
It depends entirely on the one who wields it.

00:14:45.110 --> 00:14:45.980
This is foolishness.

00:14:46.780 --> 00:14:48.990
Well, right now, I'm sure it is.

00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:51.910
Jin, if at some point in the future,

00:14:51.910 --> 00:14:56.370
ye find the resolve to fight against what's within you, come see me!

00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:03.000
How you've grown...

00:15:04.090 --> 00:15:06.760
I'm going to look for Major Kisaragi.

00:15:06.760 --> 00:15:08.670
Do you have some idea where he might be?

00:15:09.670 --> 00:15:11.890
Ragna the Bloodedge...

00:15:11.890 --> 00:15:14.470
What?! The SS-class wanted criminal?

00:15:14.720 --> 00:15:15.560
Yeah.

00:15:15.560 --> 00:15:18.680
Thinking back now, that was when he started acting like he is now...

00:15:22.440 --> 00:15:25.020
Man, so that really was him...

00:15:25.020 --> 00:15:29.030
Oh, I'm such an idiot! Why did I leave him?!

00:15:29.240 --> 00:15:31.950
If I'd waited, Major Kisaragi might have...

00:15:31.950 --> 00:15:35.370
Give the Kaka Clan village on the lowest level a look.

00:15:35.370 --> 00:15:37.870
You just might be able to find the person you're looking for.

00:15:37.870 --> 00:15:39.120
The Kaka Clan?

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:40.620
Listen to me, Noel.

00:15:40.620 --> 00:15:43.460
If you run into Tsubaki, call me.

00:15:43.460 --> 00:15:45.880
Whatever you do, don't do anything rash.

00:15:45.880 --> 00:15:47.000
Makoto?

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:50.970
I'm sure if we sit down and talk it through, the three of us can go make it work out.

00:15:50.970 --> 00:15:51.680
Okay.

00:15:59.180 --> 00:16:00.680
That uniform...

00:16:01.640 --> 00:16:03.060
Which way?

00:16:03.060 --> 00:16:04.060
Ars magus!

00:16:05.110 --> 00:16:06.110
It's this way.

00:16:06.360 --> 00:16:07.360
Hold it right there.

00:16:09.820 --> 00:16:11.360
What? Wh-Who are you?

00:16:11.360 --> 00:16:13.950
I am Litchi Faye-Ling. I practice medicine in this town.

00:16:14.320 --> 00:16:16.490
Wh-What's a doctor doing with a weapon?

00:16:16.780 --> 00:16:20.080
What business does a member of the NOL's Praetorian Guard have beyond this point?

00:16:20.290 --> 00:16:23.040
Uh, um, I'm looking for someone.

00:16:23.040 --> 00:16:25.540
He has white hair and wears red.

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:27.840
I see. I thought as much.

00:16:27.840 --> 00:16:29.500
You know him?

00:16:29.500 --> 00:16:34.470
Yes. As well as the reason why
the NOL wants to take his life.

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:38.600
No matter who they may be, it's a doctor's duty to protect their patients!

00:16:38.600 --> 00:16:40.180
P-Please wait a minute.

00:16:40.180 --> 00:16:42.730
I-It's true that I'm a member of the Praetorian Guard,

00:16:42.730 --> 00:16:45.730
but the reason I'm looking for him has nothing to do with my duties!

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:47.440
Then, what <i>is</i> your reason?

00:16:47.440 --> 00:16:53.030
He saved me and I owe him my life, but we parted ways earlier.

00:16:54.200 --> 00:16:55.610
You two are enemies, aren't you?

00:16:55.610 --> 00:16:59.910
No! Well, we're sort of on opposite sides, but he...

00:16:59.910 --> 00:17:02.700
Um, he feels familiar somehow...

00:17:02.700 --> 00:17:05.580
I have to see him!

00:17:05.580 --> 00:17:09.040
Or else, bad things will happen
to the people I care about!

00:17:09.040 --> 00:17:11.420
Please believe me! I'm begging you!

00:17:13.260 --> 00:17:15.180
Oh hell no!

00:17:15.180 --> 00:17:18.390
You have to eat lots or you won't get better!

00:17:18.600 --> 00:17:21.180
I ate! I ate plenty!

00:17:22.310 --> 00:17:24.310
There are limits to these things!

00:17:24.850 --> 00:17:27.310
What's the commotion for? You sure seem lively.

00:17:27.310 --> 00:17:30.650
Oh? Didn't Boobie Lady go home already?

00:17:30.860 --> 00:17:32.940
That was my intention, yes.

00:17:33.860 --> 00:17:34.780
It's you...

00:17:34.780 --> 00:17:36.280
Uh, um...

00:17:36.280 --> 00:17:39.490
Something came up, and I absolutely had to see you.

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:40.830
Something came up, huh?

00:17:40.830 --> 00:17:43.410
Hey! Your bandages have been undone!

00:17:43.410 --> 00:17:44.000
Oh...

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:46.660
Tao, I told you to make sure to watch after him, didn't I?!

00:17:46.660 --> 00:17:48.210
I <i>was</i> watching him!

00:17:48.210 --> 00:17:51.670
I told him, but Good Guy took them off himself!

00:17:51.670 --> 00:17:53.550
It's going to take a while
for these wounds to completely—

00:17:56.800 --> 00:17:57.840
You're kidding.

00:17:58.130 --> 00:17:59.800
What was that about my wounds?

00:18:02.930 --> 00:18:05.480
What the hell? Quit ogling me.

00:18:05.480 --> 00:18:07.640
I-I wasn't looking!

00:18:07.640 --> 00:18:09.350
Yeah, sure you weren't!

00:18:09.350 --> 00:18:10.400
Oh?

00:18:10.400 --> 00:18:12.610
I had thought to come save you,

00:18:13.320 --> 00:18:14.980
but perhaps there was no need.

00:18:14.980 --> 00:18:16.110
Wh-Who are you?

00:18:16.110 --> 00:18:18.030
You smell good!

00:18:18.030 --> 00:18:19.490
You damn Rabbit!

00:18:19.740 --> 00:18:22.450
You're... Miss Rachel?

00:18:22.830 --> 00:18:25.250
Sustaining injuries upon injuries...

00:18:25.250 --> 00:18:26.410
It's pathetic.

00:18:26.410 --> 00:18:28.620
Whose fault do you think that is?!

00:18:28.620 --> 00:18:31.250
You're the one who left me rotting there!

00:18:31.250 --> 00:18:34.090
My house has become so animeowted!

00:18:34.090 --> 00:18:36.130
No fair, Tao!

00:18:36.130 --> 00:18:37.880
We wanna play, too!

00:18:37.880 --> 00:18:38.880
Wanna play!

00:18:38.880 --> 00:18:40.050
What?
Wanna!

00:18:40.050 --> 00:18:42.050
O-Ow! Ow! Owowow!

00:18:42.050 --> 00:18:44.060
It still hurts!

00:18:44.060 --> 00:18:46.930
I wants to play! I wants to play!

00:18:46.930 --> 00:18:50.690
You seem to know a lot about him, little miss.

00:18:51.020 --> 00:18:52.400
You will refer to her as "lady"!

00:18:52.400 --> 00:18:53.820
You're being way too familiar!

00:18:53.820 --> 00:18:56.780
The object of your long search is finally right before your eyes.

00:18:56.780 --> 00:18:58.400
How does it feel?

00:18:58.820 --> 00:19:00.360
Litchi Faye-Ling.

00:19:00.740 --> 00:19:02.320
H-How did you know that?

00:19:02.320 --> 00:19:04.080
Who in the world are you?

00:19:04.240 --> 00:19:08.000
Well, I am an old acquaintance of Kokonoe's.

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:10.040
Perhaps I will just leave it at that.

00:19:10.210 --> 00:19:11.250
Of the Profesor's?

00:19:12.000 --> 00:19:15.460
I swear! They all just had to come barging in here!

00:19:18.420 --> 00:19:20.380
Hey, I'm not a frickin' zoo animal!

00:19:20.380 --> 00:19:21.010
I...

00:19:21.340 --> 00:19:24.220
I can't apply the bandages if I don't look!

00:19:24.390 --> 00:19:25.930
Oh wow, terrific excuse!

00:19:27.810 --> 00:19:29.230
Ow!

00:19:29.770 --> 00:19:33.650
So, why did you have to see me again?

00:19:35.730 --> 00:19:39.110
What is your relationship with Major Jin Kisaragi?

00:19:39.360 --> 00:19:40.820
You're asking about Jin?

00:19:42.740 --> 00:19:45.120
He's my enemy. Isn't it obvious?

00:19:45.120 --> 00:19:46.870
I know that!

00:19:46.870 --> 00:19:49.080
But that's not all. There's something else...

00:19:49.870 --> 00:19:51.410
What do you think it is?

00:19:51.410 --> 00:19:54.500
I-I don't know. That's why I'm here asking you.

00:19:54.500 --> 00:19:56.250
Jeez, you're weird.

00:19:56.250 --> 00:19:58.550
I'm an enemy to you, too.

00:19:58.550 --> 00:20:00.300
I-I...

00:20:00.300 --> 00:20:01.760
You saw it, too, didn't you?

00:20:02.010 --> 00:20:03.220
The Cauldron.

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:09.220
I'm going to smash that Cauldron, the NOL that's trying to stop me...

00:20:09.220 --> 00:20:12.520
...and above all, that bastard Terumi.

00:20:12.520 --> 00:20:16.060
Um, by Terumi, you mean Mr. Hazama, right?

00:20:16.060 --> 00:20:17.020
But why?

00:20:17.020 --> 00:20:19.690
"Why"? "Why", you ask?

00:20:19.690 --> 00:20:22.030
None of your frickin' business, that's why!

00:20:24.990 --> 00:20:27.870
What's this? You're not gonna
run away crying this time?

00:20:27.870 --> 00:20:29.370
N-No, I'm not leaving.

00:20:29.370 --> 00:20:32.580
Because there's the matter
concerning Major Kisaragi, too.

00:20:32.580 --> 00:20:37.000
If I don't ask you now,
I think I'll regret it later for sure.

00:20:37.340 --> 00:20:39.710
You must be tired from your long trip, Cap—

00:20:40.300 --> 00:20:43.050
Special Advisor Hazama. Engineer Relius.

00:20:43.050 --> 00:20:44.840
Why, thank you.

00:20:47.260 --> 00:20:50.680
The 13th Hierarchical City of Kagutsuchi.

00:20:50.680 --> 00:20:51.560
That is right.

00:20:51.850 --> 00:20:55.020
All the players are in the process of gathering here.

00:20:57.400 --> 00:20:59.610
Hey, that part doesn't need any bandages!

00:21:03.280 --> 00:21:05.700
Wait for me, Brother.

00:21:06.570 --> 00:21:08.950
I'll be there soon to kill you.

00:21:12.200 --> 00:21:17.460
Despair, disappointment, hatred, sorrow, heartbreak...

00:21:17.670 --> 00:21:22.920
I'll get to see the faces of all kinds of people writhing in the depths of their suffering.

00:23:01.520 --> 00:23:04.980
This time, we have the voice actress of Noel Vermillion, Kondou Kanako...

00:23:04.980 --> 00:23:06.530
And the voice actess
of Makoto Nana—

00:23:06.530 --> 00:23:08.780
Episode 5,
"The Pair of White Guns."

00:23:09.030 --> 00:23:10.530
The voice actress
of Makoto Nanaya...
